{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790421242,"nonce":"L4kdt2kG85YmcMVDfm6mCNnnw/I=","title":"Python: a local joined from int, float, bool and None is a run-time number, not a box","message":"Wave-2 package P-num-representation (perf-designs-2026-09-21, track_python-typing). A local assigned two or more of int, float, bool and None joins to Ty::Num(mask) instead of Object: the value struct (tag, int, float) with Lua's tags (NONE 0, FALSE 1, TRUE 2, INT 3, FLOAT 4). Relates to a42aae4 (chaos fields boxed because Int and Float join to Object).\n\nScope of this package:\n- Ty::Num lattice (Ty::num, Ty::mask, join, join_local), made only for locals of a body that no nested body shares; globals, cells, parameters, returns, fields, tuple and dict shapes and list elements still read a Num as Object (P-num-fields-lists widens them).\n- Typer::expr gives the boxed view; Typer::expr_num keeps Num for the readers that compute on it: assignment to local names, augmented assignment, arithmetic operands.\n- Lowering: coerce between Num and int/float/bool/None/Object (zb_num_box, zb_num_tag_in, zb_num_int, zb_num_float in zyntax_builtins dynamic.rs); truthiness, `is None`, and + - * on the parts (float result when a side is a float, int when both are within bool|int, otherwise both paths computed and selected). Every other reader takes the box, which the dynamic layer handles as before.\n- '%d' of a dynamic value truncates a float as the typed path does (zb_any_pct_int), and raises TypeError for a non-number.\n- ZYNTAX_DISABLE_NUM=1 restores the Object join.\n\nLeft for P-num-arith and later: / // % ** and comparisons on the parts, Num-\u003eInt for __index__ contexts with CPython's texts, zb_num_str/repr/hash/eq (the box gives the same answers), the type_traces test harness.\n\nDynamic-layer message gaps found while pinning the cases (not Num-specific, present before): `None + 1` says \"unsupported operand type(s): 'NoneType' and 'int'\" (CPython adds \"for +:\"); `xs[1.0]` says \"'float' object cannot be interpreted as an integer\" (CPython: \"list indices must be integers or slices, not float\"); `\"ab\" * 1.0` the same (CPython: \"can't multiply sequence by non-int of type 'float'\"); `'%d' % \"s\"` on a typed str prints s; format(x, \"d\") is not compiled.","files":null}]}